                                        "sense_id": "8027cf5c-38fa-33eb-9368-69673d927a6b",
                                        "entry_id": "a2784736-5faa-315b-968a-85c46a5461e9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Initialism of Canadian Survey Ship (the designation for a survey ship operated by the Canadian Hydrographic Service)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "countable",
                                            "initialism",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "87151e53-faa4-3120-a539-3a03c68cb7c9",
                                        "entry_id": "a2784736-5faa-315b-968a-85c46a5461e9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Initialism of cascading style sheet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "countable",
                                            "initialism",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1be565a8-8625-4534-8272-5a2928dbf294",
                                                "sense_id": "87151e53-faa4-3120-a539-3a03c68cb7c9",
                                                "text": "One needs only to decide upon a series of rules to define the functionality of a CSS and then to decide how to implement that sheet, either directly within their HTML document, or by using an externally linked file."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "114ada7e-3227-40bc-a3d9-36b4bc7ec6db",
                                                "sense_id": "87151e53-faa4-3120-a539-3a03c68cb7c9",
                                                "text": "A marked-up document can have a CSS linked to it, but a user may have a CSS on their machine that will override it, which can cause problems sometimes and can need checking where publishers need to be sure the content is accurately presented."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "170082b3-28f4-4a4e-838a-bc1ad7d1d747",
                                                "sense_id": "87151e53-faa4-3120-a539-3a03c68cb7c9",
                                                "text": "Now, the first thing we will do is to alter our listing page to respect the layout of the original Agendatech, importing the CSSs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d6a2e85-d432-4e33-b0ea-11bb8c3fc5bd",
                                                "sense_id": "87151e53-faa4-3120-a539-3a03c68cb7c9",
                                                "text": "Create a CSS with the following rules: a. Set the text color for the page to \"#ff6600\", and the text color for <h1> to \"IndianRed\"."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1ca5f810-6d17-36b6-b280-26b95a73b30d",
                                        "entry_id": "a2784736-5faa-315b-968a-85c46a5461e9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Initialism of control stick steering, a method of Space Shuttle flight control."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "countable",
                                            "initialism",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "97dd521c-f78f-39cb-9157-751776a83306",
                                        "entry_id": "a2784736-5faa-315b-968a-85c46a5461e9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Initialism of critical swim speed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "countable",
                                            "initialism",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2dc8f011-ffff-38df-9254-61a32f1112ee",
                                        "entry_id": "a2784736-5faa-315b-968a-85c46a5461e9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Initialism of chromosome substitution strain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "countable",
                                            "initialism",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5fddb5a9-a426-4677-82e6-9441abe9d4a6",
                                                "sense_id": "2dc8f011-ffff-38df-9254-61a32f1112ee",
                                                "text": "Recently, the construction of CSS has been reported for the mapping of a susceptibility locus for testicular cancer on mouse chromosome 19."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "09983b5f-b5fc-4395-8e10-f2c4b77f279a",
                                                "sense_id": "2dc8f011-ffff-38df-9254-61a32f1112ee",
                                                "text": "However, the gender of the mice, and, hence, the “direction” of the cross, is important to ensure that the X and Y chromosomes and the mitochondria are derived from the host strain in autosomal CSSs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0aaae06f-9e25-414c-87b0-c0686fda5799",
                                                "sense_id": "2dc8f011-ffff-38df-9254-61a32f1112ee",
                                                "text": "CSS models are also advantageous for detecting a given QTL in the presence of many other QTLs. In comparing results of published mapping studies, as many, and usually substantially more, QTLs were detected with CSSs than with F₂ intercrosses of comparable size."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
